A||N||10||janak||Fiero Newbie||||6||
Z||000000||janak||03-24-2000||05:56 AM||||Hello, I am a Fiero Newbie. My friend is trading me his 87 four cylinder Fiero for my battered up Datsun 280ZX. I have another 280ZX which I love, so he can have it. I just want to know more about the car, what I should be aware of, ect. In short, I want a crash course in fieros. Any information you can give me will be greatly appreciated.<P>Joe||||reg||6
Z||000001||sdm1964||03-24-2000||06:31 AM||||Good trade, there is no crash course that we can give you. Things go wrong with a car over 10 years old, we are here to help. Some common things i see are, headlights don't go up or down, Factory exaust manifolds are junk and are prone to cracking, Weired coolant fill procedures. But there are some rules in the forum you have to obey, 1. Have to post a pic of the car. 2 Have to tell us more about yourself, how old, where from, etc. 3 Have to set the rice burner on fire 4. Be real carefull how you word things or several forum members will get ya, Right monkeyman!!!!  Sit back and watch over 800 crazy people in love with a little peice of plastic..... Wecome to the family||||reg||7
Z||000002||DJRice||03-24-2000||08:43 AM||||Crash?  Crash is bad!  No crash the Fiero!<P>Welcome to the forum.  The search function is a good way to get familiar with a lot of stuff.  Just dream up a keyword and search for it, and if you dont find the info you need, just ask.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||03-24-2000||10:41 AM||||Welcome to the Forum.  It's always nice to hear from new folks.<P>I thoroughly enjoy driving and looking at my 85SE v-6 4spd.  I haven't gotten tired of it in 3 years.<P>The most annoying thing about Fieros is all the unfounded rumors that all the experts spread.  These are people who know the entire history of the Fiero but have never even seen one in person much less driven one.<P>Like SDM1964 said, Fieros have the same problems that most 12 to 16 year old cars with over 100000 miles on them have.  What most other cars don't have is this Forum to lean on for help.<P>When I travel I always call the local Fiero folks and meet them. So far I've been very pleased with the warm reception.<P>Again welcome to the Forum and good luck with your new Fiero.<P>Carroll<P>||||reg||7
Z||000004||ounmongk||03-24-2000||01:10 PM||||<BR>One, last thing... you're going to develop an addiction for driving this car. So be warned: "a sunday drive might last until next friday!"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> And with what everyone else has said, this is a great place for learning about your car... when I first got my fiero, a lack of knowledge and a web search led me to this forum... ever since then, I think I can know when my baby is feeling bad, or needs something, you'll learn alot here. Also, for future reference, the 4-cyl is called an iron duke ( or as we four-bangers like to call 'em) Iron Ducks.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> one last thing... don't batter this car like that  280SXof yours, okay?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> good luck||||reg||1
Z||000005||Motorhead||03-24-2000||01:23 PM||||Welcome janak.  Like you, I also own a "rice burner" of the same make and model as yours, but we don't use that kind of language here. It's an '83.  <P>This is absolutely the best group of car nuts I've ever seen, with a vast amount of knowledge.  Feel free to ask ANYTHING, there are no dumb questions, just varying degrees of expertise on this one of a kind car.<P>Guess what kind of motorcycle I own.  Yes it burns rice also.  I DO own a Sears garden tractor though, American made, well, most of it.     ||||reg||10
Z||000006||Motorhead||03-24-2000||01:29 PM||||Careful ounmongk!  ZX owners take offense when you refer to their cars as SX's.||||reg||1
Z||000007||DRH||03-24-2000||01:37 PM||||Welcome aboard!<P>Here are a couple of Fiero sites on the web with links to quite a few sites. You can spend days going thru this stuff (not to mention the links you find as you go).<BR> <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/</A>   ( Click on Fiero Secrets )<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/1930/wwfl.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/1930/wwfl.html</A> <P><BR>Happy surfing!||||reg||1
Z||000008||Monkeyman||03-25-2000||10:48 AM||||janak--Welcome.  You are about to become one of the elite.  (Only 370,xxx Fieros built)  Feel free to ask any questions.  There are some pretty handy folks around here.  As one of the least knowledgable, but most obsessed Fieroholics here, do as sdm1964 says.  Take pics, ask questions and by all means, whatever you do...<B>DO NOT TALK TRASH ABOUT MY FIEROS!!</B>  (Yes, I claim all 370,xxx of them as mine! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)<P>sdm1964--I had an ex wife who was in love with a little piece of plastic.  (BTW-She didn't drive a Fiero.  'Nuff said on a family forum!)||||reg||1
Z||000009||janak||03-25-2000||05:41 PM||||Thanks for the reception guys. I should have my hands on the wheel early next week. I can't wait. I have always liked the Fiero, even though I dont really care for the "Victims of American Engineering" that were so common in the 80's and early 90's. Thats why I went Datsun. I still have an 81, which is my baby, but I want an all out sports car, hence the Fiero. I will take some pics and post them ASAP. I can post a pic of my "Rice-Burner" if you really want to see it. I my self am 21, a history major, and an avid car nut. Anything else you want to know, just ask. <P>Joe||||reg||14
Z||000010||Ozzy||03-26-2000||04:24 AM||||Welcome, Enjoy!<P>I want to know if you can find me a 12 step program for Fiero's!!<P>I bought an '88 Coupe 4 cyl a little over a year ago. I have threatened to set it alight several times but most of the problems were in fact small.<P>I now have the Coupe, a '84 SE 2M4 (parts car and about to sell) and I just brought home a blue '87 GT today!!! (HELP!!!!!!)<P>Just kidding...this forum and it's members have saved me much time and $$$$. In my opinion, this is the most usefull Fiero site amongst the hundreds I've seen on the web. I hope you enjoy your Fiero and this forum.<P>Ozzy||||reg||1
